**Two Sum** (LeetCode 1): given an integer array `nums` and a `target`, return the indices of the two numbers that add up to `target`. Assumes exactly one valid answer exists and the same element can't be used twice.

**Approach:** Scan once with a hash map from value to index. For each element `x`, check whether `target - x` is already in the map; if so, return the pair, otherwise store `x`.

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution
{
    public int[] TwoSum(int[] nums, int target)
    {
        var seen = new Dictionary<int, int>();
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.Length; i++)
        {
            int need = target - nums[i];
            if (seen.TryGetValue(need, out int j))
                return new[] { j, i };
            seen[nums[i]] = i;
        }
        return System.Array.Empty<int>();
    }
}
```

`target - nums[i]` can overflow if values are near `int.MinValue`/`int.MaxValue`; use `long` for the subtraction if the constraints allow such values.

